    "translation": "ts_opus_nolessons",
    "file": "baselines/ts_runs_v2/opus_nolessons/witnesses.lean",
    "line": 96,
    "eq": "(x : Nat) : FAPPLY (FEMPTY : fmap Nat Nat) x = ARB"
   },
   {
    "translation": "ts_sonnet",
    "file": "baselines/ts_runs_v2/sonnet_lessons/witnesses.lean",
    "line": 33,
    "eq": "FAPPLY (FEMPTY : FMap Nat Nat) 0 = FAPPLY (FEMPTY : FMap Nat Nat) 1"
   },
   {
    "translation": "ts_sonnet",
    "file": "baselines/ts_runs_v2/sonnet_lessons/witnesses.lean",
    "line": 109,
    "eq": "FAPPLY (FEMPTY : FMap Nat Nat) 5 = locncol .EOFpt"
   }
  ],
  "note": "Witnesses: FAPPLY FEMPTY 0 = ARB (opus), FAPPLY FEMPTY x = ARB for every x (nolessons), FAPPLY FEMPTY 0 = FAPPLY FEMPTY 1 and FAPPLY FEMPTY 5 = locncol EOFpt (sonnet). All have f = FEMPTY, so P holds; keys x = 0, 1, 5, any x are not restricted (P is type-generic; x is polymorphic).",
  "doubt": "HOL4 FAPPLY is a defined constant: FAPPLY_DEF (finite_mapScript.sml:180) says FAPPLY f x = OUTL (fmap_REP f x), so off the domain the value is the single closed term OUTL (INR one) for every f and x, not a free value. Saved theorem NOT_FDOM_FAPPLY_FEMPTY (line 562: ~(x IN FDOM f) ==> f ' x = FEMPTY ' x) ties all off-domain values together, and FAPPLY_DEF itself mentions the constant. A replacement with P = `f = FEMPTY` and a g that depends on f will therefore break NOT_FDOM_FAPPLY_FEMPTY (and FAPPLY_DEF) for reasons that say nothing about the witnesses; a consistent test needs P = `~(x IN FDOM f)` (P_wide) and g independent of f (e.g. g x), and FAPPLY_DEF must be excluded from the check or restated. Lean fixes the off-domain value of every map and key, so P_wide is also the region the Lean definition fixes.",
  "P_wide": "~(x IN FDOM f)",
  "type_instance": "",
  "hol4_source": "E:/ts_ws/hol4src/src/finite_maps/finite_mapScript.sml:180",
  "vary_note": "HOL4 defines FAPPLY f x = OUTL (fmap_REP f x); FEMPTY maps every x to INR one, so OUTL is varied on INR values and FAPPLY co-varies.",
  "covary": [
   {
    "const": "finite_map$FAPPLY",
    "term": "\\(f:'a |-> 'b) (x:'a). OUTL (fmap_REP f x)"
   }
  ]
 },
